    "q-159366": {
      "dom_id": "step-q159366",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider two random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=6,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=7,$ mixed moment $\\text{E}[XY]=40,$ and variances $\\text{Var}[X]=2$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=5.$ Find the covariance matrix for $X$ and $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "For two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ the covariance matrix $Σ$ is given by\n\n$$\nΣ=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & \\text{Cov}[X,Y] \\\\ \\text{Cov}[Y,X] & \\text{Var}[Y]\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nUsing the above formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =40-6\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nΣ=[\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & \\text{Cov}[X,Y] \\\\ \\text{Cov}[Y,X] & \\text{Var}[Y]\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
